he shop assistant refuse to serve Dickie?","start":12.08,"end":15.59,"score":0.936,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-002","sourceId":"b3-031-002","sourceIndex":1,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,11],"wordModel":"english-ctc-fallback","text":"True eccentrics never deliberately set out to draw attention to themselves.","start":18.18,"end":23.05,"score":0.975,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-003","sourceId":"b3-031-003","sourceIndex":2,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,13],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"They disregard social conventions without being conscious that they are doing anything extraordinary.","start":23.85,"end":29.72,"score":0.988,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-004","sourceId":"b3-031-004","sourceIndex":3,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,21],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"This invariably wins them the love and respect of others, for they add colour to the dull routine of everyday life.","start":30.35,"end":37.66,"score":0.947,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-005","sourceId":"b3-031-005","sourceIndex":4,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,19],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"Up to the time of his death, Richard Colson was one of the most notable figures in our town.","start":39.08,"end":44.85,"score":0.963,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-006","sourceId":"b3-031-006","sourceIndex":5,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,22],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"He was a shrewd and wealthy businessman, but most people in the town hardly knew anything about this side of his life.","start":45.64,"end":53.12,"score":0.965,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-007","sourceId":"b3-031-007","sourceIndex":6,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,18],"wordModel":"english-ctc-fallback","text":"He was known to us all as Dickie and his eccentricity had become legendary long before he died.","start":53.8,"end":61.21,"score":0.979,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-008","sourceId":"b3-031-008","sourceIndex":7,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,4],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"Dickie disliked snobs intensely.","start":62.39,"end":64.68,"score":0.864,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-009","sourceId":"b3-031-009","sourceIndex":8,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,17],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"Though he owned a large car, he hardly ever used it, preferring always to go on foot.","start":65.26,"end":70.91,"score":0.985,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-010","sourceId":"b3-031-010","sourceIndex":9,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,12],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"Even when it was raining heavily, he refused to carry an umbrella.","start":71.58,"end":75.4,"score":0.968,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-011","sourceId":"b3-031-011","sourceIndex":10,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,17],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"One day, he walked into an expensive shop after having been caught in a particularly heavy shower.","start":76.2,"end":82.81,"score":0.967,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-012-p01","sourceId":"b3-031-012","sourceIndex":11,"part":1,"parts":2,"wordRange":[0,10],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"He wanted to buy a ￡300 watch for his wife,","start":83.68,"end":87.3,"score":0.949,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-012-p02","sourceId":"b3-031-012","sourceIndex":11,"part":2,"parts":2,"wordRange":[10,25],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"but he was in such a bedraggled condition that an assistant refused to serve him.","start":87.67,"end":92.84,"score":0.979,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-013","sourceId":"b3-031-013","sourceIndex":12,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,14],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"Dickie left the shop without a word and returned carrying a large cloth bag.","start":93.42,"end":98.7,"score":0.959,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-014","sourceId":"b3-031-014","sourceIndex":13,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,11],"wordModel":"english-ctc-fallback","text":"As it was extremely heavy, he dumped it on the counter.","start":99.49,"end":102.87,"score":0.986,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-015","sourceId":"b3-031-015","sourceIndex":14,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,19],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"The assistant asked him to leave, but Dickie paid no attention to him and requested to see the manager.","start":103.76,"end":110.36,"score":0.977,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-016","sourceId":"b3-031-016","sourceIndex":15,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,15],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"Recognizing who the customer was, the manager was most apologetic and reprimanded the assistant severely.","start":111.24,"end":118.59,"score":0.979,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-017","sourceId":"b3-031-017","sourceIndex":16,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,14],"wordModel":"english-ctc-fallback","text":"When Dickie was given the watch, he presented the assistant with the cloth bag.","start":119.44,"end":123.82,"score":0.95,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-018","sourceId":"b3-031-018","sourceIndex":17,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,5],"wordModel":"english-ctc-fallback","text":"It contained ￡300 in pennies.","start":124.57,"end":128.32,"score":0.96,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-019","sourceId":"b3-031-019","sourceIndex":18,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,15],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"He insisted on the assistant's counting the money before he left--30, 000 pennies in all!","start":129.14,"end":135.45,"score":0.854,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":true,"reviewReasons":["low-word-confidence"]},{"id":"b3-031-020","sourceId":"b3-031-020","sourceIndex":19,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,18],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"On another occasion, he invited a number of important critics to see his private collection of modern paintings.","start":136.46,"end":143.14,"score":0.994,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-021-p01","sourceId":"b3-031-021","sourceIndex":20,"part":1,"parts":2,"wordRange":[0,11],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"This exhibition received a great deal of attention in the press,","start":143.98,"end":147.32,"score":0.982,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-021-p02","sourceId":"b3-031-021","sourceIndex":20,"part":2,"parts":2,"wordRange":[11,32],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"for though the pictures were supposed to be the work of famous artists, they had in fact been painted by Dickie.","start":148.06,"end":153.98,"score":0.967,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-031-022","sourceId":"b3-031-022","sourceIndex":21,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,24],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"It took him four years to stage this elaborate joke simply to prove that critics do not always know what they are talking about.","start":154.58,"end":162.88,"score":0.967,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]}]}
